{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"640a95090f5f9ee5","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is outbound traffic?**|What is outbound traffic?]]","x":-1920,"y":10324,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"8a089839c22263f2","type":"text","text":"`Outbound traffic` is traffic going out from your VPC to the internet or another network.  \nExample:\n```\nEC2 instance → Internet\n```","x":-1520,"y":10346,"width":500,"height":165},
		{"id":"eaefdac52f046090","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is inbound traffic?**|What is inbound traffic?]]","x":-1920,"y":10549,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"26875bf3050cd609","type":"text","text":"`Inbound traffic` is traffic coming into your VPC from the internet or another network.  \nExample:\n```\nInternet user → Public web server\n```","x":-1520,"y":10549,"width":500,"height":165},
		{"id":"8fcf5964f21e2a67","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What are data transfer rates?**|What are data transfer rates?]]","x":-1920,"y":10774,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"f207db5a53ca9192","type":"text","text":"`Data transfer rates` are costs charged based on how much data moves in or out.  \nFor example, AWS may charge for data transfer from your VPC to the internet.  ","x":-1520,"y":10774,"width":500,"height":120},
		{"id":"af4105164781c832","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is external internet traffic?**|What is external internet traffic?]]","x":-1920,"y":9844,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"2b49e2946c9ab61d","type":"text","text":"`External internet traffic` is traffic coming from outside AWS.  \nFor example:\n```\nUser browser → Internet → Your public web server in AWS\n```\nThis is inbound traffic from the public internet.  ","x":-1520,"y":9844,"width":500,"height":234},
		{"id":"f852f3c2e492f7e2","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is internet-bound traffic?**|What is internet-bound traffic?]]","x":-1920,"y":10094,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"bb749697c2988285","type":"text","text":"`Internet-bound traffic` is traffic going to the internet.  \nFor example:\n```\nPrivate EC2 instance → NAT Gateway → Internet\n```\nThis is outbound traffic from your VPC to the internet.  ","x":-1520,"y":10094,"width":500,"height":190}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"6dec08a06b674801","fromNode":"af4105164781c832","fromSide":"right","toNode":"2b49e2946c9ab61d","toSide":"left"},
